{"id": "1545628258777698344", "channel_id": "1545385622317965442", "author_id": "1389806015561728032", "author_name": "topcat.0001_40485", "content": "Free pulls doesn’t change design direction. \n\nThese difficulty spikes are intended. I highly doubt they even adjusted the numbers prior to launch. These numbers according to light is essentially the benchmarks for madness story difficulty. and will continue to become more apparent in other game modes.\n\nThrowing out candy to appease the peasants is a tried and true method for scummy gacha games.\n\nVarious gacha games do this same pattern constantly (Lilith Afk arena comes to mind) granted most of them have larger audiences so they can survive bad public reception from time to time.\n\nMorimens is rather niche and has has a small population. The game has survived largely on word of mouth rather than Biavs marketing failures.", "timestamp": "2026-09-05T02:54:53.277000+00:00", "thread_id": "1545385622317965442", "thread_title": "On the D-Effect Zone Adjustments", "forum_channel_id": "1184003940082262069"}
